# SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS.vec -- OVMX's SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS.EXE, the shareable image
# through which an image LINKed on real OpenVMS Alpha reaches the system
# services (rd vms-3b3f). SINGLE SOURCE for this image's symbol vector.
#
# An Alpha image calls a system service through a linkage pair that names
# the service by its BYTE OFFSET in SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS' symbol vector (16
# bytes per entry). Each offset below is OBSERVED: it is the value the link
# map of our own probe program (tools/lab-alpha/probes/ORDS.MAR, linked on the
# lab OpenVMS Alpha V8.4 node) reports for that universal; the full observed
# table is docs/oracle/alpha84-symvec-offsets.txt. Clean-room: nothing here
# comes from a VSI/HPE binary or source.
#
# Each entry is a null-frame procedure that transfers, arguments untouched,
# to the OVMX universal named in the third column, in LIBVMS$SHR. An
# UPPER-CASE target takes the VMS argument forms (descriptors, item lists:
# src/libvms/syssvc/sys_vmsabi.c). A lower-case target is OVMX's own service,
# listed only where every argument is a value or the address of a value or
# buffer whose layout is the same for a 32-bit-pointer VMS caller (event flag
# numbers, masks, quadword times, an AST routine and its parameter). Every
# other slot is a retired (PRIVATE) entry, so an image that calls one fails to
# activate honestly (%IMGACT-I-NOTIMPL) instead of reaching a routine that
# misreads its arguments. Each listed entry is exercised by an image LINKed
# on the lab node (tests/native-images/alpha/sp/, the semantic-oracle probes).
#
# GSMATCH: images record the ident of the SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS they were linked
# against (major 51, minor 16699012, match EQUAL -- observed in every captured
# image's global section descriptor), so OVMX's carries that ident.
#
#   gsmatch EQUAL,51,16699012
#   use     LIBVMS$SHR.EXE
#   use     LIBVMSRMS$SHR.EXE
#
# The rights-database slots (0xA50-0xA70, vms-8b5) are observed in the link map
# of the rights probe (tests/native-images/alpha/sp/SP_RIGHTS.MAP.txt), $CHKPRO
# (0xAB0) in that of the $CHKPRO probe (SP_CHKPRO.MAP.txt), and the RMS slots
# (0x6D0-0x860) in that of the RMS probe (SP_RMS.MAP.txt): those go to the
# VMS-layout FAB/RAB/NAM entry points in LIBVMSRMS$SHR (src/vmsrms/rms_vmsabi.c);
# $FINISH_RDB is OVMX's own service in LIBVMSRMS$SHR (a context longword's
# address is its one argument).
#
# offset  universal        OVMX target
0x080     SYS$QIOW         SYS$QIOW
0x0E0     SYS$ASCEFC       SYS$ASCEFC
0x0F0     SYS$ASCTIM       SYS$ASCTIM
0x100     SYS$ASSIGN       SYS$ASSIGN
0x120     SYS$BINTIM       SYS$BINTIM
0x130     SYS$CANCEL       sys$cancel
0x140     SYS$CANTIM       sys$cantim
0x1A0     SYS$CLREF        sys$clref
0x1E0     SYS$CREMBX       SYS$CREMBX
0x1F0     SYS$CREPRC       SYS$CREPRC
0x210     SYS$DACEFC       sys$dacefc
0x230     SYS$DASSGN       SYS$DASSGN
0x270     SYS$DELMBX       sys$delmbx
0x280     SYS$DELPRC       SYS$DELPRC
0x2C0     SYS$DLCEFC       SYS$DLCEFC
0x2F0     SYS$EXIT         sys$exit
0x310     SYS$FAO          SYS$FAO
0x320     SYS$FAOL         SYS$FAOL
0x330     SYS$FORCEX       SYS$FORCEX
0x340     SYS$IMGSTA       SYS$IMGSTA
0x380     SYS$HIBER        sys$hiber
0x3F0     SYS$SNDOPR       SYS$SNDOPR
0x400     SYS$QIO          SYS$QIO
0x410     SYS$READEF       sys$readef
0x420     SYS$RESUME       SYS$RESUME
0x450     SYS$SETAST       sys$setast
0x460     SYS$SETEF        sys$setef
0x4A0     SYS$SETIMR       sys$setimr
